For every ket $\ket{A}$ there is a corresponding vector in the dual space, written $\bra{A}$. The map from ket to bra is additive but conjugates complex scalars: $\begin{aligned}
  \ket{A}+\ket{B}
  &\longleftrightarrow
  \bra{A}+\bra{B},\\
  z\ket{A}
  &\longleftrightarrow
  z^*\bra{A}.
  \end{aligned}$ This second rule is the essential complex feature. The dual of a scalar multiple is multiplied by the complex conjugate scalar.

