p.src:
For the two-component realization, $\ket{\alpha}
  =
  \begin{pmatrix}
    \alpha_1\\
    \alpha_2
  \end{pmatrix}
  \qquad\Longrightarrow\qquad
  \bra{\alpha}
  =
  \begin{pmatrix}
    \alpha_1^*&\alpha_2^*
  \end{pmatrix}.$ Complex conjugation implements the dual correspondence, and the row notation keeps the two kinds of object visibly distinct. Equation  also verifies Equation  directly.

